Recently, i have been giving a lot of thought about various things
that can be fixed about nethack. I am not a programmer, so i don't
know what kind of work any of these fixes will entail, but i thought
since i have the ideas i might as well right about them to see if
anything comes out of them. The things that concern me are: The way
that the game seems unwinable without reading spoilers, Lack of class
differences by the end game, the uselessness of some weapon
artifacts, lack of responses of #chat (there should be more), and The
really awful way the oracle talks. (you can be obtuse without being
awkward.) 

This Yani is only going to address classes. 

I was reading the faq on the nethack homepage under the section of
adding new classes. The dev team thinks that the classes are not even
different enough right now and i agree with them. This is what i
think should be done. 

Before i start however, here i the guidelines i want to keep in mind. 
Play balance. I don't want to change play balance over all if i can
help it. If one class is made harder(or easier) i am not too
concerned about it.  Not all classes are considered the same in
difficulty as it stands right now.  

How the game looks to newbies and the unspoiled vs expert players.
Even though i consider myself an expert player, i am most concerned
about how the game is played from the eyes of the less experienced. I
want to keep it fun for them, and anything that is abusive or
unbalanced from an experts or spoiled players  point of view is not
really what   I focus on.  I realize because i am thoroughly spoiled
i won't succeed very well at this task. 

 Spells. Not all the characters should be able to use spells. As it
stands right now anybody can become a spell caster with a robe and
high enough lvl and intelligence/wisdom. Of course, for the unspoiled
i don't think that this is even realized so this is mostly a fix for
the expert players. I don't think this will affect beginners or the
unspoiled since most don't even know what it takes to max out their
spell casting levels. 

doors, chest and traps. keys and credit cards will only unlock doors
now.  They will  automatically set off any traps unless untrapped
first. untrapping chest or doors is now only allowed to T,A,and R.
Rogues get a this message on the first chest or door trap they would
have normally set off in the game. There is a trap here. Do you want
to untrap it? (#untrap). T,A and R get better at untrapping when
raising exp level. Rogues will have a higher chance at success.  You
need a lock pick to untrap chest or doors. credit cards can only be
used by T,A,R. You need a lock pick to open locked chest. The kick
and force command works the same as it does now. There is a new
prompt for all characters the first time they try to open a locked
chest. This is locked! Do you want to try to bust it? (#force or
#kick) . Note, spell casting wands and untrapping dungeon  traps work
the same as they 
do now. 

